{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774711,"nonce":"etMxqe0ZIWtb6OPSZoT/imx6W/c=","title":"ADR-0043: launch parameters + manual dispatch (World B), + ADR-0044 allowed_refs fix","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #16 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/adr-0037-allowed-refs-branch` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-16T05:55:43Z · Merged: 2026-07-16T06:22:28Z\n\nImplements **ADR-0043** (launch parameters + manual dispatch as a repo-aware trigger) end-to-end, plus **ADR-0044** (a governance correctness fix surfaced during the work). Delivers the \"show a pipeline's mandatory/optional parameters in the Run-Pipeline flow\" ask — reframed from a UI feature into the IR/launch-layer gap it actually was.\n\nBuilt as a stack of tracer-bullet slices, each verified (build + tests) before the next.\n\n\n**ADR-0043 — launch parameters**\n- **Slice 1** — typed `interface.inputs` (`ParamSpec`: `string`/`boolean`/`number`/`choice`, static `required`, `default`, `validate:` CEL), unified across `invoke` and launch. Pure `coerce`/`resolve_params`/`validate_param_specs`; `inputs` bound on the ADR-0041 CEL rail; `SCARAB_PARAM_*` env; params frozen on the run (`runs.params`) → restart-safe. Backward-compatible bare-string deserialize. Supplied via inline `POST /v1/runs`.\n- **Slice 2** — manual/API dispatch as a repo+ref-aware trigger (\"World B\"): `on: manual`/`on: api` opt-in, `dispatch_run` + `POST /v1/repos/{org}/{repo}/dispatch`, ref→SHA pinning, shared read-at-ref/compile/admission with the webhook path, params fail-closed before run creation, Environment governance intact.\n- **Slice 3** — `GET …/pipelines?ref=` catalog + `GET …/pipelines/{name}/interface?ref=` describe (compiled typed specs + resolved SHA), and a working `scarab run \u003corg\u003e/\u003crepo\u003e \u003cpipeline\u003e --param k=v` — UI and CLI share one validator (server-side coercion).\n- **Slice 4** — SolidJS Run-Pipeline flow: catalog → typed form (widget per type, ★ mandatory / optional-prefilled), static-only client validation (no client CEL), inline per-param server errors, re-run prefill. Exposes non-secret `params` on the run detail.\n\n**ADR-0044 — `allowed_refs` fix (governance correctness)**\n- Environment `allowed_refs` was glob-matched against the commit **SHA** (via `config_ref`), never a branch, so branch-scoped deploy gating was a no-op — a pre-existing bug on the webhook path that dispatch would have inherited.\n- Adds `Event::protection_ref()` (symbolic branch/tag ref) distinct from the immutable read/pin ref; matches `allowed_refs` against it at **both** enforcement points (creation-time admit + gate-approval re-check). PR → `refs/pull/N/head` (fail-safe); dispatch canonicalizes `main` → `refs/heads/main`. Regression tests confirmed failing pre-fix.\n\n`cargo build --workspace` clean; per-crate test suites green (pipeline/engine/server/forge/testkit; DB-gated suites skip without `SCARAB_TEST_DATABASE_URL` but compile). UI `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` succeeds. `openapi.json` regenerated and in sync.\n\n- Re-run prefills params only (run record lacks pipeline/ref).\n- UI dispatch path isn't E2E-tested; its error parsing couples to the server's plain-text error shape.\n- `${{ inputs.* }}` doesn't resolve inside `concurrency.group` yet (no interpolation rail there).\n\nTracked in-repo via git-bug: `ba20e88`, `0a3b098`, `44f8c65`, `019a64e`, `8183ade` (all closed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}